  "notes": "An onomatopoeic word ({擬態語|ぎたいご}) describing a wet, slimy, slippery texture. Often carries a slightly unpleasant nuance — the feel of algae, raw fish, or a grimy surface.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ぬるぬるする: to be/feel slimy\n- ぬるぬるした: slimy (adjective-like)\n- ぬるぬるの〜: slimy ~ (noun modifier)\n\nTYPICAL THINGS DESCRIBED:\n- {魚|さかな}: fish\n- {海藻|かいそう}: seaweed\n- お{風呂|ふろ}の{床|ゆか}: bathroom floor\n- {石鹸|せっけん}: soap\n\nSIMILAR TEXTURE WORDS:\n- ねばねば: sticky, gooey (like natto)\n- つるつる: smooth and slippery (positive nuance)\n- べたべた: sticky (like sugar or sweat)\n- ぬめぬめ: slimy (very close synonym, slightly milder)",
